      "title": "Trump’s suggestion that Iran could ‘take out’ LA or San Diego draws Republican rebuke",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/06/republican-trump-iran-los-angeles-san-diego",
      "description": "<p>Congressional candidate Jim Desmond says he ‘served to protect Americans, not write off American cities’</p><p>A <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans\">Republican</a> candidate in San Diego has criticized <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump\">Donald Trump</a> after the US president <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/06/trump-suggests-let-iran-take-out-los-angeles-san-diego\">suggested</a> Iran could “take out” the city or Los Angeles.</p><p>Trump has faced a chorus of condemnation from Democratic leaders in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california\">California</a> after his comments at a rally in Nebraska on Monday night. Republicans have largely remained silent.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/06/republican-trump-iran-los-angeles-san-diego\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
